      "worked": "Yes. Take $f(x)=kx^2+(2k+1)x+(k+1)$, where $k\\ne0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(2k+1)^2-4k(k+1)\\\\\\Delta&=4k^2+4k+1-4k^2-4k\\\\\\Delta&=1.\\end{align*}$$\n\nAll three coefficients depend on $k$, while the discriminant is independent of $k$. The restriction $k\\ne0$ ensures the function is quadratic.",
